          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kapota \"a dove, a pigeon\" is old, in the Rigveda, and is inherited from Indo-Iranian (EtymDB). Its cousin is Persian kabūtar \"pigeon\", which Hindi and Urdu took from Persian, so the Hindi pigeon is a Persian cousin of this Sanskrit word."
            }
          ]
        },
