              "text": "bhramara \"a large black bee\" is filed by MW under the root √bhram \"wander, whirl\", which MW compares with Greek bremō and Latin fremere \"roar, hum\" (EtymDB gives an Indo-European root \"make noise\"). It lives on as Hindi bhaũrā \"black bee\" (CDIAL 9651)."
